    "created_at": "2025-11-13T16:59:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-13T16:59:09Z",
    "body": "It turns out that this is worse thank I thought. The async call to apply the history step falls down into the wait for all making several scroll tests not spec correct as well. Basically all tests doing\n```\nawait navigation.back().finished\nassert_true(some scrolling condition) \n```\nare wrong, and needs an `await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 0))` before the assert to have a chance to be spec compliant, even though that is probably not enough.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3528785670/reactions",
